.TH TPM-PIN-CTL 1 "November 2026" "tpm-pin 1.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tpm-pin-ctl \- manage TPM 2.0 hardware-backed PIN authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpm-pin-ctl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpm-pin-ctl
is the command-line administration and enrollment tool for
.BR pam_tpm_pin (8).
It seals per-user master keys inside the system TPM 2.0 under a user PIN
(optionally bound to UEFI Secure Boot PCR 7), optionally seals the user's
verified login password for automatic GNOME Keyring / KWallet unlocking, and
manages PAM integration and TPM Dictionary Attack (DA) protection.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [\-\-json] [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Display TPM 2.0 availability, hardware architecture, PIN enrollment state,
PCR 7 binding, keyring status, PAM integration, active policies, and live
hardware DA lockout counters.
.TP
.B enroll [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Enroll or re-enroll a TPM-backed PIN for the target user (requires root).
When
.I enable_keyring_unlock
is enabled, prompts for the user's current login password, verifies it
against the local shadow database when available, and seals it with AES-256-GCM
under the TPM-protected master key.
.TP
.B change-pin [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Verify the user's current PIN against the TPM, preserve any previously sealed
login password, and re-seal a new PIN (requires root).
.TP
.B verify [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Verify an enrolled PIN against the TPM 2.0 device and report whether any sealed
keyring password can be unsealed.
.TP
.B remove [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Securely overwrite and remove the enrolled PIN blob for the target user
(requires root).
.TP
.B list [\-\-json]
List enrolled users, UIDs, PCR 7 binding, and keyring auto-unlock flags.
When invoked as root, lists all enrolled users on the system; otherwise reports
only the calling user.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-json] [\-\-user \fIusername\fP]
Run diagnostic health checks covering TPM device status, DA lockout state,
setuid helper permissions, PAM module installation and activation, Polkit
systemd drop-in status, data directory permissions, config-vs-blob drift,
and keyring PAM module detection. Exits 0 if no failures are detected, or 1 if
any check fails.
.TP
.B pam <enable|disable [\-\-uninstall]|status>
Enable, disable, or inspect system PAM integration across supported Linux
distributions (Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora/RHEL/authselect, Arch Linux, openSUSE,
and generic PAM stacks). Enabling and disabling require root.
.TP
.B da-reset
Clear the TPM 2.0 Dictionary Attack lockout counter (requires root).
.TP
.B da-config \-\-max-tries \fIn\fP \-\-recovery-sec \fIs\fP [\-\-lockout-recovery \fIs\fP]
Configure hardware TPM DA limits and persist them to
.I /etc/tpm-pin/config.conf
(requires root).
.TP
.B config list [\-\-json]
Print all active configuration keys and values.
.TP
.B config get \fIkey\fP
Print the current value of a single configuration key.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
Update and save a configuration key (requires root).
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR, \fB\-V\fR, \fBversion\fR
Print the program version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Configuration is stored in
.IR /etc/tpm-pin/config.conf :
.TP
.B digits_only
Boolean. Restrict PINs to ASCII digits 0\-9 (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B min_length\fR, \fBmax_length
Integer (4\-64). Minimum and maximum PIN byte length (defaults: \fB4\fP, \fB32\fP).
.TP
.B disallow_simple_pins
Boolean. Reject sequential (\fB1234\fP, \fB4321\fP) and repeating
(\fB1212\fP, \fB123123\fP) PINs during enrollment and PIN rotation
(default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B enable_login
Boolean. Allow PIN at local display managers and console login (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B enable_lockscreen
Boolean. Allow PIN for desktop screen lockers (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B enable_sudo
Boolean. Allow PIN for \fBsudo\fP, \fBdoas\fP, and \fBsu\fP (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B enable_polkit
Boolean. Allow PIN for graphical Polkit / \fBpkexec\fP prompts (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B enable_keyring_unlock
Boolean. Seal the login password in the TPM to auto-unlock GNOME Keyring or
KWallet on login (default: \fBtrue\fP).
.TP
.B bind_pcr7
Boolean. Seal keys to UEFI Secure Boot PCR 7 (default: \fBfalse\fP).
.TP
.B da_max_tries\fR, \fBda_recovery_time\fR, \fBda_lockout_recovery
Integers controlling TPM hardware anti-hammering thresholds and cooldowns
(defaults: \fB5\fP, \fB600\fP, \fB86400\fP).
.TP
.B tcti_name\fR, \fBdata_dir
Optional TCTI override string and credential storage directory
(default: \fI/var/lib/tpm-pin\fP).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tpm-pin/config.conf
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tpm-pin/<uid>/sealed.blob
Root-only (\fB0600\fP) TPM-sealed master key and AES-256-GCM payload.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tpm-pin/<uid>/sealed.meta
Non-sensitive enrollment flags (\fB0644\fP) for unprivileged status queries.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns \fB0\fP on success and non-zero on failure. For \fBdoctor\fP, returns
\fB1\fP if one or more checks report \fBfail\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam_tpm_pin (8),
.BR tpm-pin-settings (1)
